Subject: [ZEROX] Restore legacy TNT and world settings on upgrade

ZEROX v2/v3 wrote behavior-changing values into persistent configuration files.
Restoring Java source defaults in v4 did not modify those existing files, so upgraded
servers could remain limited to 16 or 32 primed TNT ticks per tick.

This patch adds a one-time, exact-value migration when semantic-preserving mode is active:

- `spigot.yml`: `max-tnt-per-tick: 16|32` -> `100`
- `config/paper-world-defaults.yml`: armor-stand collision lookup `false` -> `true`
- `config/paper-world-defaults.yml`: pathfinding-on-block-update `false` -> `true`
- force `tnt.load-shedding-enabled=false`
- force `plugins.defer-repeating-tasks=false`

Only exact values previously shipped by ZEROX are migrated. Every changed file is backed
up under `.zerox/backups/` before replacement, and a one-time migration marker is stored
in `.zerox/zerox.properties`.

The regression test starts from a legacy configuration, requires automatic migration and
backup creation, then ignites TNT and verifies no ZEROX deferral is emitted.
